IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `cpp-core`
IMPORT `cpp-core-calendar`
IMPORT `cpp-core-age`
IMPORT `cp5-months`
IMPORT `cp5-d-retirement`

-- Tests of sections 67 and 68 (cp5-d-retirement.l4).
-- Every expected value was worked out by hand from the text of the section, before the code was run, and is
-- written beside its assertion. Section 2(2) makes "the month in which a person reached an age" the month AFTER
-- the month of the birthday (a person born on 15 June 1960 reaches 60 in July 2020 and 65 in July 2025).
-- A month is written as the first day of the month.

§ `Tests of sections 67 and 68`

§§ `Fixtures`

-- An application by a person who is not an estate, with the facts the tests vary and the other facts absent.
GIVEN dob IS A DATE
      received IS A DATE
      approved IS A MAYBE DATE
      chosen IS A MAYBE DATE
      ceased IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A `cp5 Application for a retirement pension`
`cp5 test fixture -- an application` dob received approved chosen ceased MEANS
    `cp5 Application for a retirement pension` WITH
        `the applicant is an estate` IS FALSE
        `date of birth of the applicant` IS dob
        `day the application was received` IS received
        `day payment of the pension was approved` IS approved
        `a day in the month the contributor last worked and for which a contribution was made` IS NOTHING
        `a day in the last month for which unadjusted pensionable earnings were attributed under section 55` IS NOTHING
        `a day in the month the applicant chose for the pension to commence` IS chosen
        `day the applicant wholly or substantially ceased paid employment and self-employment` IS ceased

-- The same, for the pre-1987 rule, which reads the last month worked and the last month with earnings attributed.
GIVEN dob IS A DATE
      received IS A DATE
      worked IS A MAYBE DATE
      attributed IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A `cp5 Application for a retirement pension`
`cp5 test fixture -- an application under the old rule` dob received worked attributed MEANS
    `cp5 Application for a retirement pension` WITH
        `the applicant is an estate` IS FALSE
        `date of birth of the applicant` IS dob
        `day the application was received` IS received
        `day payment of the pension was approved` IS JUST received
        `a day in the month the contributor last worked and for which a contribution was made` IS worked
        `a day in the last month for which unadjusted pensionable earnings were attributed under section 55` IS attributed
        `a day in the month the applicant chose for the pension to commence` IS NOTHING
        `day the applicant wholly or substantially ceased paid employment and self-employment` IS NOTHING

-- An application by an estate, otherwise like the first one above.
`cp5 test fixture -- an estate's application` MEANS
    `cp5 Application for a retirement pension` WITH
        `the applicant is an estate` IS TRUE
        `date of birth of the applicant` IS YearMonthDay 1960 6 15
        `day the application was received` IS YearMonthDay 2020 9 10
        `day payment of the pension was approved` IS JUST (YearMonthDay 2020 10 1)
        `a day in the month the contributor last worked and for which a contribution was made` IS NOTHING
        `a day in the last month for which unadjusted pensionable earnings were attributed under section 55` IS NOTHING
        `a day in the month the applicant chose for the pension to commence` IS NOTHING
        `day the applicant wholly or substantially ceased paid employment and self-employment` IS NOTHING

-- A person born on 15 June 1960: reaches 60 in July 2020, 65 in July 2025, 70 in July 2030.
`cp5 test person born 15 June 1960` MEANS YearMonthDay 1960 6 15
-- A person born on 15 June 1950: reaches 60 in July 2010, 65 in July 2015, 70 in July 2020.
`cp5 test person born 15 June 1950` MEANS YearMonthDay 1950 6 15

§§ `Subsection 67(3.1): a pension that commences on or after 1 January 2012`

-- Under 65 when applying: the later of the month the applicant reached 60 and the month after the month of application.
-- Applied 10 Sep 2020 at 60: (a) July 2020, (b) October 2020. Latest: October 2020.
#ASSERT `s 67(3.1) — the month a retirement pension that commences on or after 2012 is first payable` (`cp5 test fixture -- an application` `cp5 test person born 15 June 1960` (YearMonthDay 2020 9 10) (JUST (YearMonthDay 2020 10 1)) NOTHING NOTHING) EQUALS JUST (YearMonthDay 2020 10 1)
-- A month chosen in the application that is later governs: January 2021.
#ASSERT `s 67(3.1) — the month a retirement pension that commences on or after 2012 is first payable` (`cp5 test fixture -- an application` `cp5 test person born 15 June 1960` (YearMonthDay 2020 9 10) (JUST (YearMonthDay 2020 10 1)) (JUST (YearMonthDay 2021 1 10)) NOTHING) EQUALS JUST (YearMonthDay 2021 1 1)
-- A chosen month that is earlier than October 2020 does not bring the pension forward.
#ASSERT `s 67(3.1) — the month a retirement pension that commences on or after 2012 is first payable` (`cp5 test fixture -- an application` `cp5 test person born 15 June 1960` (YearMonthDay 2020 9 10) (JUST (YearMonthDay 2020 10 1)) (JUST (YearMonthDay 2020 8 5)) NOTHING) EQUALS JUST (YearMonthDay 2020 10 1)
-- Applied 30 June 2020: not reached 60 until 1 July; (a) July 2020 and (b) July 2020 (the month after June).
#ASSERT `s 67(3.1) — the month a retirement pension that commences on or after 2012 is first payable` (`cp5 test fixture -- an application` `cp5 test person born 15 June 1960` (YearMonthDay 2020 6 30) (JUST (YearMonthDay 2020 7 1)) NOTHING NOTHING) EQUALS JUST (YearMonthDay 2020 7 1)
-- Applied well before 60 (1 March 2020): (b) April 2020 is earlier than (a) July 2020, so July 2020.
#ASSERT `s 67(3.1) — the month a retirement pension that commences on or after 2012 is first payable` (`cp5 test fixture -- an application` `cp5 test person born 15 June 1960` (YearMonthDay 2020 3 1) (JUST (YearMonthDay 2020 7 1)) NOTHING NOTHING) EQUALS JUST (YearMonthDay 2020 7 1)
-- One day before the person is treated as reaching 65 (30 June 2025): still under 65, so (b) July 2025.
#ASSERT `s 67(3.1) — the month a retirement pension that commences on or after 2012 is first payable` (`cp5 test fixture -- an application` `cp5 test person born 15 June 1960` (YearMonthDay 2025 6 30) (JUST (YearMonthDay 2025 7 1)) NOTHING NOTHING) EQUALS JUST (YearMonthDay 2025 7 1)
-- On 1 July 2025 the person has reached 65: (c) is the eleventh month before July 2025 (August 2024), but not before July 2025.
#ASSERT `s 67(3.1) — the month a retirement pension that commences on or after 2012 is first payable` (`cp5 test fixture -- an application` `cp5 test person born 15 June 1960` (YearMonthDay 2025 7 1) (JUST (YearMonthDay 2025 7 1)) NOTHING NOTHING) EQUALS JUST (YearMonthDay 2025 7 1)
-- Applied 20 Aug 2025 (65 reached): (c) is September 2024, not earlier than July 2025: July 2025.
#ASSERT `s 67(3.1) — the month a retirement pension that commences on or after 2012 is first payable` (`cp5 test fixture -- an application` `cp5 test person born 15 June 1960` (YearMonthDay 2025 8 20) (JUST (YearMonthDay 2025 9 1)) NOTHING NOTHING) EQUALS JUST (YearMonthDay 2025 7 1)
-- Applied 5 Dec 2026: the eleventh month before December 2026 is January 2026, which is after July 2025.
#ASSERT `s 67(3.1) — the month a retirement pension that commences on or after 2012 is first payable` (`cp5 test fixture -- an application` `cp5 test person born 15 June 1960` (YearMonthDay 2026 12 5) (JUST (YearMonthDay 2027 1 1)) NOTHING NOTHING) EQUALS JUST (YearMonthDay 2026 1 1)
-- Boundary of the eleventh month: applied 5 Dec 2026, retroactivity ends at January 2026; applied 5 Jan 2027, it ends at February 2026.
#ASSERT `s 67(3.1) — the month a retirement pension that commences on or after 2012 is first payable` (`cp5 test fixture -- an application` `cp5 test person born 15 June 1960` (YearMonthDay 2027 1 5) (JUST (YearMonthDay 2027 2 1)) NOTHING NOTHING) EQUALS JUST (YearMonthDay 2026 2 1)
-- Not approved: the section decides nothing.
#ASSERT `s 67(3.1) — the month a retirement pension that commences on or after 2012 is first payable` (`cp5 test fixture -- an application` `cp5 test person born 15 June 1960` (YearMonthDay 2020 9 10) NOTHING NOTHING NOTHING) EQUALS NOTHING
-- An estate: the subsection does not apply.
#ASSERT `s 67(3.1) — the month a retirement pension that commences on or after 2012 is first payable` `cp5 test fixture -- an estate's application` EQUALS NOTHING
-- A pension whose month falls before 2012 is not one this subsection governs (born 1950, applied Sep 2010 at 60: October 2010).
#ASSERT `s 67(3.1) — the month a retirement pension that commences on or after 2012 is first payable` (`cp5 test fixture -- an application` `cp5 test person born 15 June 1950` (YearMonthDay 2010 9 10) (JUST (YearMonthDay 2010 10 1)) NOTHING NOTHING) EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `Subsection 67(2): a pension that commences on or after 1 January 1987`

-- Applied 10 Sep 2010 at 60 and still working: (a) July 2010, (b) October 2010, (d) July 2015, the month reached 65. Latest: July 2015.
#ASSERT `s 67(2) — the month a retirement pension that commences on or after 1987 is first payable` (`cp5 test fixture -- an application` `cp5 test person born 15 June 1950` (YearMonthDay 2010 9 10) (JUST (YearMonthDay 2010 10 1)) NOTHING NOTHING) EQUALS JUST (YearMonthDay 2015 7 1)
-- Ceased work on 15 Dec 2010 at 60: (c) January 2011 replaces (d); (b) October 2010; latest January 2011.
#ASSERT `s 67(2) — the month a retirement pension that commences on or after 1987 is first payable` (`cp5 test fixture -- an application` `cp5 test person born 15 June 1950` (YearMonthDay 2010 9 10) (JUST (YearMonthDay 2010 10 1)) NOTHING (JUST (YearMonthDay 2010 12 15))) EQUALS JUST (YearMonthDay 2011 1 1)
-- Ceased work on 10 March 2016, after reaching 65: (c) does not apply (not then under 65); (d) applies (not ceased at 65): July 2015.
#ASSERT `s 67(2) — the month a retirement pension that commences on or after 1987 is first payable` (`cp5 test fixture -- an application` `cp5 test person born 15 June 1950` (YearMonthDay 2010 9 10) (JUST (YearMonthDay 2010 10 1)) NOTHING (JUST (YearMonthDay 2016 3 10))) EQUALS JUST (YearMonthDay 2015 7 1)
-- Ceased work in the month the person is treated as reaching 65: on 30 June 2015 the person is still under 65, so (c) gives July 2015.
#ASSERT `s 67(2) — the month a retirement pension that commences on or after 1987 is first payable` (`cp5 test fixture -- an application` `cp5 test person born 15 June 1950` (YearMonthDay 2010 9 10) (JUST (YearMonthDay 2010 10 1)) NOTHING (JUST (YearMonthDay 2015 6 30))) EQUALS JUST (YearMonthDay 2015 7 1)
-- A later chosen month governs: December 2016.
#ASSERT `s 67(2) — the month a retirement pension that commences on or after 1987 is first payable` (`cp5 test fixture -- an application` `cp5 test person born 15 June 1950` (YearMonthDay 2010 9 10) (JUST (YearMonthDay 2010 10 1)) (JUST (YearMonthDay 2016 12 3)) NOTHING) EQUALS JUST (YearMonthDay 2016 12 1)
-- Applied after 70 (12 May 2021; 70 reached July 2020), still working: (e) June 2020 (the twelfth month before June 2021), (f) July 2020; latest July 2020.
#ASSERT `s 67(2) — the month a retirement pension that commences on or after 1987 is first payable` (`cp5 test fixture -- an application` `cp5 test person born 15 June 1950` (YearMonthDay 2021 5 12) (JUST (YearMonthDay 2021 6 1)) NOTHING NOTHING) EQUALS JUST (YearMonthDay 2020 7 1)
-- The day before 70 is reached (30 June 2020) the applicant is under 70: (b) July 2020 and (d) July 2015, so July 2020.
#ASSERT `s 67(2) — the month a retirement pension that commences on or after 1987 is first payable` (`cp5 test fixture -- an application` `cp5 test person born 15 June 1950` (YearMonthDay 2020 6 30) (JUST (YearMonthDay 2020 7 1)) NOTHING NOTHING) EQUALS JUST (YearMonthDay 2020 7 1)
-- January 1987 rule (g): born 15 June 1925 (60 in July 1985, 65 in July 1990), applied 5 March 1986, ceased work 20 December 1985:
-- (a) July 1985, (b) April 1986, (c) January 1986, (g) January 1987. Latest: January 1987.
#ASSERT `s 67(2) — the month a retirement pension that commences on or after 1987 is first payable` (`cp5 test fixture -- an application` (YearMonthDay 1925 6 15) (YearMonthDay 1986 3 5) (JUST (YearMonthDay 1986 4 1)) NOTHING (JUST (YearMonthDay 1985 12 20))) EQUALS JUST (YearMonthDay 1987 1 1)
-- The same person if not approved gets nothing from the section.
#ASSERT `s 67(2) — the month a retirement pension that commences on or after 1987 is first payable` (`cp5 test fixture -- an application` (YearMonthDay 1925 6 15) (YearMonthDay 1986 3 5) NOTHING NOTHING (JUST (YearMonthDay 1985 12 20))) EQUALS NOTHING
-- A month before 1987 is not one this subsection governs: born 1920 (65 in July 1985), applied 10 May 1986, ceased at 65+: June 1986.
#ASSERT `s 67(2) — the month a retirement pension that commences on or after 1987 is first payable` (`cp5 test fixture -- an application` (YearMonthDay 1920 6 15) (YearMonthDay 1986 5 10) (JUST (YearMonthDay 1986 6 1)) NOTHING (JUST (YearMonthDay 1986 12 10))) EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `Subsection 67(1): a pension that commences before 1 January 1987`

-- Born 15 June 1920 (65 in July 1985), applied 10 May 1986; last worked and contributed December 1985, earnings attributed to December 1985:
-- (a) July 1985, (b) the eleventh month before May 1986 = June 1985, January 1986, January 1986. Latest: January 1986.
#ASSERT `s 67(1) — the month a retirement pension that commences before 1987 is first payable` (`cp5 test fixture -- an application under the old rule` (YearMonthDay 1920 6 15) (YearMonthDay 1986 5 10) (JUST (YearMonthDay 1985 12 20)) (JUST (YearMonthDay 1985 12 1))) EQUALS JUST (YearMonthDay 1986 1 1)
-- Last worked in May 1986: the month after is June 1986, the latest.
#ASSERT `s 67(1) — the month a retirement pension that commences before 1987 is first payable` (`cp5 test fixture -- an application under the old rule` (YearMonthDay 1920 6 15) (YearMonthDay 1986 5 10) (JUST (YearMonthDay 1986 5 2)) NOTHING) EQUALS JUST (YearMonthDay 1986 6 1)
-- Nothing worked and nothing attributed: (a) July 1985 and the eleventh month before May 1986 (June 1985): July 1985.
#ASSERT `s 67(1) — the month a retirement pension that commences before 1987 is first payable` (`cp5 test fixture -- an application under the old rule` (YearMonthDay 1920 6 15) (YearMonthDay 1986 5 10) NOTHING NOTHING) EQUALS JUST (YearMonthDay 1985 7 1)
-- A month of January 1987 or later is outside the subsection: last worked December 1986 gives January 1987.
#ASSERT `s 67(1) — the month a retirement pension that commences before 1987 is first payable` (`cp5 test fixture -- an application under the old rule` (YearMonthDay 1920 6 15) (YearMonthDay 1986 5 10) (JUST (YearMonthDay 1986 12 10)) NOTHING) EQUALS NOTHING
-- The applicant must have reached 65 (a person born 1930 has not, in 1986).
#ASSERT `s 67(1) — the month a retirement pension that commences before 1987 is first payable` (`cp5 test fixture -- an application under the old rule` (YearMonthDay 1930 6 15) (YearMonthDay 1986 5 10) (JUST (YearMonthDay 1985 12 20)) NOTHING) EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `Subsection 67(3): an applicant who attained 65 before the application was received`

-- Born 15 June 1930 (65 in July 1995), applied 10 Sep 1998: (a) the later of October 1997 and January 1995, (b) July 1995. Latest: October 1997.
#ASSERT `s 67(3) — the month a retirement pension is first payable to an applicant who attained 65 before the day the application was received` (`cp5 test fixture -- an application` (YearMonthDay 1930 6 15) (YearMonthDay 1998 9 10) (JUST (YearMonthDay 1998 9 10)) NOTHING NOTHING) EQUALS JUST (YearMonthDay 1997 10 1)
-- The floor of January 1995: born 15 June 1929 (65 in July 1994), applied 10 March 1995: the eleventh month before March 1995 is April 1994, so January 1995.
#ASSERT `s 67(3) — the month a retirement pension is first payable to an applicant who attained 65 before the day the application was received` (`cp5 test fixture -- an application` (YearMonthDay 1929 6 15) (YearMonthDay 1995 3 10) (JUST (YearMonthDay 1995 3 10)) NOTHING NOTHING) EQUALS JUST (YearMonthDay 1995 1 1)
-- Applied on the day the person is treated as reaching 65 (1 July 2025): not "before the day", so the subsection does not apply.
#ASSERT `s 67(3) — the month a retirement pension is first payable to an applicant who attained 65 before the day the application was received` (`cp5 test fixture -- an application` `cp5 test person born 15 June 1960` (YearMonthDay 2025 7 1) (JUST (YearMonthDay 2025 7 1)) NOTHING NOTHING) EQUALS NOTHING
-- Applied the day after (2 July 2025): the subsection applies; the eleventh month before July 2025 is August 2024, not later than July 2025.
#ASSERT `s 67(3) — the month a retirement pension is first payable to an applicant who attained 65 before the day the application was received` (`cp5 test fixture -- an application` `cp5 test person born 15 June 1960` (YearMonthDay 2025 7 2) (JUST (YearMonthDay 2025 7 2)) NOTHING NOTHING) EQUALS JUST (YearMonthDay 2025 7 1)
-- A chosen month later than the rest governs.
#ASSERT `s 67(3) — the month a retirement pension is first payable to an applicant who attained 65 before the day the application was received` (`cp5 test fixture -- an application` (YearMonthDay 1930 6 15) (YearMonthDay 1998 9 10) (JUST (YearMonthDay 1998 9 10)) (JUST (YearMonthDay 1999 2 1)) NOTHING) EQUALS JUST (YearMonthDay 1999 2 1)
-- Not approved: nothing.
#ASSERT `s 67(3) — the month a retirement pension is first payable to an applicant who attained 65 before the day the application was received` (`cp5 test fixture -- an application` (YearMonthDay 1930 6 15) (YearMonthDay 1998 9 10) NOTHING NOTHING NOTHING) EQUALS NOTHING

-- Subsections (3) and (3.1) give the same month for an applicant who had reached 65 when applying, from 2012
-- (the eleventh month before the application month, not earlier than the month of reaching 65): born 1950,
-- applied 10 March 2016 (65 reached in July 2015): April 2015, so July 2015 by both.
#ASSERT `s 67(3) — the month a retirement pension is first payable to an applicant who attained 65 before the day the application was received` (`cp5 test fixture -- an application` `cp5 test person born 15 June 1950` (YearMonthDay 2016 3 10) (JUST (YearMonthDay 2016 3 10)) NOTHING NOTHING) EQUALS JUST (YearMonthDay 2015 7 1)
#ASSERT `s 67(3.1) — the month a retirement pension that commences on or after 2012 is first payable` (`cp5 test fixture -- an application` `cp5 test person born 15 June 1950` (YearMonthDay 2016 3 10) (JUST (YearMonthDay 2016 3 10)) NOTHING NOTHING) EQUALS JUST (YearMonthDay 2015 7 1)
-- Applied 10 Dec 2016: the eleventh month before December 2016 is January 2016, after July 2015: both give January 2016.
#ASSERT `s 67(3) — the month a retirement pension is first payable to an applicant who attained 65 before the day the application was received` (`cp5 test fixture -- an application` `cp5 test person born 15 June 1950` (YearMonthDay 2016 12 10) (JUST (YearMonthDay 2016 12 10)) NOTHING NOTHING) EQUALS JUST (YearMonthDay 2016 1 1)
#ASSERT `s 67(3.1) — the month a retirement pension that commences on or after 2012 is first payable` (`cp5 test fixture -- an application` `cp5 test person born 15 June 1950` (YearMonthDay 2016 12 10) (JUST (YearMonthDay 2016 12 10)) NOTHING NOTHING) EQUALS JUST (YearMonthDay 2016 1 1)

§§ `Subsection 67(3.2): the requirement to apply was waived`

-- Born 15 June 1950 (70 reached July 2020); the requirement was waived on 17 March 2023: months after the waiver start April 2023,
-- and the twelve months before that (April 2022 to March 2023) all fall after July 2020: first month April 2022.
#ASSERT `s 67(3.2) — the first month for which a retirement pension is payable where the requirement to apply was waived` TRUE `cp5 test person born 15 June 1950` (YearMonthDay 2023 3 17) EQUALS JUST (YearMonthDay 2022 4 1)
-- Waived on 1 Dec 2020: the first month after is January 2021; twelve months before is January 2020, but 70 was reached in July 2020: July 2020.
#ASSERT `s 67(3.2) — the first month for which a retirement pension is payable where the requirement to apply was waived` TRUE `cp5 test person born 15 June 1950` (YearMonthDay 2020 12 1) EQUALS JUST (YearMonthDay 2020 7 1)
-- Waived in July 2021: the first month after is August 2021; twelve months before is August 2020, after July 2020.
#ASSERT `s 67(3.2) — the first month for which a retirement pension is payable where the requirement to apply was waived` TRUE `cp5 test person born 15 June 1950` (YearMonthDay 2021 7 31) EQUALS JUST (YearMonthDay 2020 8 1)
-- Not approved: nothing.
#ASSERT `s 67(3.2) — the first month for which a retirement pension is payable where the requirement to apply was waived` FALSE `cp5 test person born 15 June 1950` (YearMonthDay 2023 3 17) EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `Subsection 67(4): a disability pension has ceased`

-- Disability pension notified ceased on 1 Oct 2022; the 90th day after is 30 December 2022.
#ASSERT `s 67(4) — the application for a retirement pension is deemed to have been received in an earlier month` TRUE (YearMonthDay 2022 10 1) (YearMonthDay 2022 12 30) NOTHING
#ASSERT NOT (`s 67(4) — the application for a retirement pension is deemed to have been received in an earlier month` TRUE (YearMonthDay 2022 10 1) (YearMonthDay 2022 12 31) NOTHING)
-- A longer period the Minister allowed, to 1 March 2023.
#ASSERT `s 67(4) — the application for a retirement pension is deemed to have been received in an earlier month` TRUE (YearMonthDay 2022 10 1) (YearMonthDay 2023 3 1) (JUST (YearMonthDay 2023 3 1))
#ASSERT NOT (`s 67(4) — the application for a retirement pension is deemed to have been received in an earlier month` TRUE (YearMonthDay 2022 10 1) (YearMonthDay 2023 3 2) (JUST (YearMonthDay 2023 3 1)))
-- The pension must have ceased for one of the two reasons.
#ASSERT NOT (`s 67(4) — the application for a retirement pension is deemed to have been received in an earlier month` FALSE (YearMonthDay 2022 10 1) (YearMonthDay 2022 10 5) NOTHING)
-- Born 15 June 1960; disability application made 12 March 2015; last month payable August 2022; applied within the 90 days:
-- (a) March 2015, (b) August 2022, (c) the month before July 2020, June 2020. Latest: August 2022.
#ASSERT `s 67(4) — the month in which the application for a retirement pension is deemed to have been received` TRUE (YearMonthDay 2022 10 1) (YearMonthDay 2022 12 15) NOTHING (YearMonthDay 2015 3 12) (YearMonthDay 2022 8 20) `cp5 test person born 15 June 1960` EQUALS JUST (YearMonthDay 2022 8 1)
-- Born 15 June 1950; disability application made 1 May 2005; last month payable February 2008: (c) June 2010 (the month before July 2010) is the latest.
#ASSERT `s 67(4) — the month in which the application for a retirement pension is deemed to have been received` TRUE (YearMonthDay 2008 4 1) (YearMonthDay 2008 5 15) NOTHING (YearMonthDay 2005 5 1) (YearMonthDay 2008 2 10) `cp5 test person born 15 June 1950` EQUALS JUST (YearMonthDay 2010 6 1)
-- Out of time and no longer period allowed: not covered.
#ASSERT `s 67(4) — the month in which the application for a retirement pension is deemed to have been received` TRUE (YearMonthDay 2022 10 1) (YearMonthDay 2023 1 15) NOTHING (YearMonthDay 2015 3 12) (YearMonthDay 2022 8 20) `cp5 test person born 15 June 1960` EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `Section 67 as a whole`

-- Born 15 June 1960, applied 10 Sep 2020, approved: (3.1) governs, October 2020.
#ASSERT `s 67 — the month a retirement pension is first payable` (`cp5 test fixture -- an application` `cp5 test person born 15 June 1960` (YearMonthDay 2020 9 10) (JUST (YearMonthDay 2020 10 1)) NOTHING NOTHING) NOTHING EQUALS JUST (YearMonthDay 2020 10 1)
-- Born 1950, applied 10 Sep 2010 at 60, still working: (3.1) does not apply (October 2010 is before 2012); (2) gives July 2015 (NOTES.md, fork F2).
#ASSERT `s 67 — the month a retirement pension is first payable` (`cp5 test fixture -- an application` `cp5 test person born 15 June 1950` (YearMonthDay 2010 9 10) (JUST (YearMonthDay 2010 10 1)) NOTHING NOTHING) NOTHING EQUALS JUST (YearMonthDay 2015 7 1)
-- Born 1950, applied 12 May 2021 after 70: (3.1) governs and gives June 2020, not (2)'s July 2020.
#ASSERT `s 67 — the month a retirement pension is first payable` (`cp5 test fixture -- an application` `cp5 test person born 15 June 1950` (YearMonthDay 2021 5 12) (JUST (YearMonthDay 2021 6 1)) NOTHING NOTHING) NOTHING EQUALS JUST (YearMonthDay 2020 6 1)
-- Born 1930, applied 10 Sep 1998: (3) governs, October 1997, not (2)'s October 1998.
#ASSERT `s 67 — the month a retirement pension is first payable` (`cp5 test fixture -- an application` (YearMonthDay 1930 6 15) (YearMonthDay 1998 9 10) (JUST (YearMonthDay 1998 9 10)) NOTHING NOTHING) NOTHING EQUALS JUST (YearMonthDay 1997 10 1)
-- Born 1925, applied 5 March 1986 at 60, ceased work in December 1985: (2), January 1987.
#ASSERT `s 67 — the month a retirement pension is first payable` (`cp5 test fixture -- an application` (YearMonthDay 1925 6 15) (YearMonthDay 1986 3 5) (JUST (YearMonthDay 1986 4 1)) NOTHING (JUST (YearMonthDay 1985 12 20))) NOTHING EQUALS JUST (YearMonthDay 1987 1 1)
-- Born 1920, applied 10 May 1986, last worked and contributed December 1985: (1), January 1986.
#ASSERT `s 67 — the month a retirement pension is first payable` (`cp5 test fixture -- an application under the old rule` (YearMonthDay 1920 6 15) (YearMonthDay 1986 5 10) (JUST (YearMonthDay 1985 12 20)) (JUST (YearMonthDay 1985 12 1))) NOTHING EQUALS JUST (YearMonthDay 1986 1 1)
-- The requirement to apply waived on 17 March 2023: (3.2) governs.
#ASSERT `s 67 — the month a retirement pension is first payable` (`cp5 test fixture -- an application` `cp5 test person born 15 June 1950` (YearMonthDay 2023 3 17) (JUST (YearMonthDay 2023 3 17)) NOTHING NOTHING) (JUST (YearMonthDay 2023 3 17)) EQUALS JUST (YearMonthDay 2022 4 1)
-- A case no subsection settles: born 1920, applied 10 May 1986, last worked and contributed December 1986 -- (1) would give January 1987 and (2) June 1986.
#ASSERT `s 67 — the month a retirement pension is first payable` (`cp5 test fixture -- an application under the old rule` (YearMonthDay 1920 6 15) (YearMonthDay 1986 5 10) (JUST (YearMonthDay 1986 12 10)) NOTHING) NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
-- Not approved: nothing.
#ASSERT `s 67 — the month a retirement pension is first payable` (`cp5 test fixture -- an application` `cp5 test person born 15 June 1960` (YearMonthDay 2020 9 10) NOTHING NOTHING NOTHING) NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `Section 68: how long a retirement pension is paid`

-- The pension is paid for the month of death and not after it.
#ASSERT `s 68 — the last month for which a retirement pension is paid` (JUST (YearMonthDay 2025 8 31)) EQUALS JUST (YearMonthDay 2025 8 1)
#ASSERT `s 68 — the last month for which a retirement pension is paid` NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 68 — a retirement pension is paid for a month` (YearMonthDay 2025 8 1) (YearMonthDay 2025 7 1) (JUST (YearMonthDay 2025 8 31))
#ASSERT NOT (`s 68 — a retirement pension is paid for a month` (YearMonthDay 2025 9 1) (YearMonthDay 2025 7 1) (JUST (YearMonthDay 2025 8 31)))
-- A beneficiary still living: paid for every month from the first.
#ASSERT `s 68 — a retirement pension is paid for a month` (YearMonthDay 2040 1 1) (YearMonthDay 2025 7 1) NOTHING
-- Not paid for a month before the first month payable.
#ASSERT NOT (`s 68 — a retirement pension is paid for a month` (YearMonthDay 2025 6 1) (YearMonthDay 2025 7 1) NOTHING)
